 "counting": "A mutant is effective when its anchor matches once, the tree compiles, the selector executes, a named test fails and the file restores byte-identically. Compile errors, crashes (a linker crash included), timeouts and runs that execute no test never count; such a run is repeated and only the repeat is recorded. The three functions do not exist on v0.7.0, so there is no baseline on the previous tag: every mutant is a mutation of new code. failing_tests lists the failing tests of a run (at most the first 12). result is the whole list replayed on the lane's machine on replay_commit; no replay ran on a separate machine. The checkouts use CRLF line endings: the runner matches on LF-normalized text and writes the file back with its own line endings. The mutated builds ran without -D warnings. Every restore is verified per mutant by SHA-256 equality (sha256_original equals sha256_restored). The selector is run green before the first mutant and after the last of each of the three shards, not after every mutant.",
